C*******************************************************************************
C			CalSimHydro Rainfall-Runoff Model Main Input File
C
C*****************************************************************************
C                            File Description
C
C  *Listed below are all input  file names used when running CalSimHydro
C   
C  *Each file name has a maximum length of 100 characters
C  
C
C---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
C   Scenario Name (to be used in Part F of pathnames in SV File
C---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  L2015A					 /SCENARIO
C---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
C    FILE NAME                                      DESCRIPTION
C---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 .\1a_RainfallRunoff\LUBySoilTypePCN.dat			         / 1: Input data file containing Land Use by Soil Type
 .\1a_RainfallRunoff\Parameter.dat             	                 / 2: Input data file containing simulation parameters   
 .\1a_RainfallRunoff\Precip.dat					 / 3: Input DSS data file containing Precipitation Data
  MonthlyPrecip.dss				 / 4: Monthly precipitation DSS output File
  EffPrecip.dss					 / 5: Effective Monthly Precipitation Output File
  UnitInfOutput.dss	 	                 / 6: Output DSS file  
C*******************************************************************************
C                         Model Simulation Period and Output
C
C   The following lists the simulation beginning time, ending time and time step length.  
C
C   BDT    ; Beginning simulation date and time. Use MM/DD/YYYY_hh:mm format. 
C             * Midnight is 24:00
C   EDT   ; Ending simulation date and time.  Use MM/DD/YYYY_hh:mm format. 
C            * Midnight is 24:00
C   CACHE   ; Cache size in terms of number of values stored for time series data output
C
C-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
C       VALUE                   DESCRIPTION
C-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
     09/30/1920_24:00           / BDT 
     09/30/2015_24:00           / EDT
     1DAY                       / UNITT
     5000000                    / CACHE
     1MON						/ UNITTOUTPUT
C*******************************************************************************
C******************************************************************************
C******************************************************************************
C                         Physical System
C
C    NREGN  ; Number of sub-regions modeled in the system
C
C-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
C       VALUE                   DESCRIPTION
C-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
         40                      / NREGN
         22                      / NLUCodes
C******************************************************************************
C*******************************************************************************
C                       Land Use Codes (Agricultural plus NV and UR)
C   
C   The following lists the codes for each agricultural crop, NV, and UR.  These codes are 
C   used during the print-out of the simulation results.
C
C    *Note* DO NOT enter codes for urban and native vegetation
C    
C--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
C
C   CCODE; Crop code (max. 5 characters)
C
C--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
C   VALUE                        DESCRIPTION
C--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
     AL		/ CCODE1	ALFALFA
     AP		/ CCODE2	ALMONDS AND PISTACHIO
     CO		/ CCODE3	COTTON
     CR		/ CCODE4	CORN
     CU		/ CCODE5	CUCURBITS
     DB		/ CCODE6	DRY BEANS
     FI		/ CCODE7	OTHER FIELD
     GR		/ CCODE8	GRAIN
     NV		/ CCODE9	Native Vegetation
     OG		/ CCODE10	ONIONS AND GARLIC
     OR		/ CCODE11	OTHER DECID.
     PA		/ CCODE12	PASTURE
     PO		/ CCODE13	POTATOES
     RI		/ CCODE14	RICE
     SB		/ CCODE15	SUGAR BEETS
     SF		/ CCODE16	SAFFLOWER
     SO		/ CCODE17	SUBTROPICAL
     TH		/ CCODE18	FRESH TOMATOES
     TM		/ CCODE19	PROCESS TOMATOES
     TR		/ CCODE20	OTHER TRUCK
     UR		/ CCODE21   URBAN
     VI		/ CCODE22	VINEYARDS                              
